You can be honest.

255
00:12:20,656 --> 00:12:21,532
US?

256
00:12:21,615 --> 00:12:24,452
-You guys want to build a snowman?
-Another one?

257
00:12:24,535 --> 00:12:27,496
It'll be fun. I had a blast building mine.

258
00:12:28,497 --> 00:12:29,957
Wanna build one next to mine?

259
00:12:30,040 --> 00:12:32,626
-We could have a contest.
-Let's go together. Right now.

260
00:12:32,710 --> 00:12:33,711
-Okay.
-All right.

261
00:12:33,794 --> 00:12:35,546
-Shall we?
-Let's go.

262
00:12:35,629 --> 00:12:37,673
Am I gonna be freezing in only this?

263
00:12:44,972 --> 00:12:47,183
Maybe red would be good for the eyes?

264
00:12:47,808 --> 00:12:49,643
BELL PEPPERS ACQUIRED

265
00:12:50,227 --> 00:12:51,771
CUCUMBER ACQUIRED

266
00:12:55,274 --> 00:12:56,942
-Here we go.
-It's freezing.

267
00:12:57,026 --> 00:12:58,027
THE SNOWMAN CREW HEADS OUT

268
00:12:58,611 --> 00:13:00,905
Oh, wow. That's big.

269
00:13:00,988 --> 00:13:05,075
-We just need to beat Kian's.
-This is a great spot here.

270
00:13:05,159 --> 00:13:06,619
Let's go.

271
00:13:06,702 --> 00:13:08,204
BUILDING IT NEXT TO THE STAFF'S SNOWMAN

272
00:13:08,287 --> 00:13:11,165
You think yours can be bigger than ours?

273
00:13:11,248 --> 00:13:13,542
No question.

274
00:13:14,210 --> 00:13:15,669
Is the base big enough?

275
00:13:15,753 --> 00:13:17,588
Let's just gather the snow first.

276
00:13:17,671 --> 00:13:19,048
-Pile it here?
-Here?

277
00:13:19,131 --> 00:13:22,134
-Yeah.
-Oh, yeah. We got this.

278
00:13:22,635 --> 00:13:24,261
This is great cardio.

279
00:13:25,387 --> 00:13:27,139
-Just pile it up.
-Okay.

280
00:13:28,516 --> 00:13:30,267
THE OWNER ALSO KEEPS ADDING TO IT

281
00:13:30,351 --> 00:13:31,435
Let's make it fatter.

282
00:13:31,519 --> 00:13:32,520
PAT PAT

283
00:13:33,729 --> 00:13:35,189
PAT PAT

284
00:13:35,272 --> 00:13:37,149
Almost back to where it was.

285
00:13:37,233 --> 00:13:38,275
PAT PAT

286
00:13:38,859 --> 00:13:40,945
PATTING IT CAREFULLY WITH HIS HANDS

287
00:13:41,028 --> 00:13:44,448
This is a competitive group.

288
00:13:44,532 --> 00:13:48,744
-We're all in on height.
-Great job, you guys. Okay.

289
00:13:48,828 --> 00:13:51,705
The more you do this,
the more addictive it becomes.

290
00:13:51,789 --> 00:13:53,123
-You guys tired?
-Oops.

291
00:13:53,207 --> 00:13:54,959
OH COME ON

292
00:13:55,042 --> 00:13:57,378
-Haven't even warmed up.
-Just getting started.

293
00:13:57,461 --> 00:13:59,755
-You guys tired?
-Oh, no way.

294
00:14:02,258 --> 00:14:04,051
PAT PAT PAT PAT PAT

295
00:14:04,969 --> 00:14:06,053
There, good as new.

296
00:14:06,136 --> 00:14:07,388
THE SNOWMAN'S GOTTEN EVEN BIGGER

297
00:14:07,471 --> 00:14:09,932
It's looking really tall.

298
00:14:10,015 --> 00:14:12,142
-Great!
-It's pretty big already.

299
00:14:12,226 --> 00:14:13,727
-Really?
-Yeah.

300
00:14:13,811 --> 00:14:15,646
-We already win on height.
-Really?

301
00:14:15,729 --> 00:14:17,606
-We caught up.
-Oh, good.

302
00:14:18,190 --> 00:14:20,484
-Can I share my opinion?
-Huh?

303
00:14:21,068 --> 00:14:23,195
It looks like a giant, white turd.

304
00:14:23,279 --> 00:14:25,614
I think it looks like ice cream.
Soft serve.

305
00:14:25,698 --> 00:14:27,533
-That's a nicer description.
-You're not wrong.

306
00:14:27,616 --> 00:14:29,451
-This is fun.
-So much fun.

307
00:14:29,535 --> 00:14:31,829
I've never enjoyed
playing in the snow this much.

308
00:14:31,912 --> 00:14:34,498
ENJOYING WINTER TO THE FULLEST
AT KIAN'S B&B

309
00:14:35,207 --> 00:14:36,458
Gonna make you handsome.

310
00:14:40,921 --> 00:14:42,673
THE SNOWMAN'S GOTTEN PRETTIER

311
00:14:42,756 --> 00:14:45,134
Okay, we still need to finish strong.

312
00:14:45,217 --> 00:14:46,260
-Oh, yeah.
-Wow.

313
00:14:46,343 --> 00:14:47,720
You like it?

314
00:14:49,555 --> 00:14:50,848
PLOPPING DOWN

315
00:14:50,931 --> 00:14:53,017
Wow. They built that thing fast.

316
00:14:53,100 --> 00:14:55,519
-It's looking good.
-Not bad.

317
00:14:55,603 --> 00:14:57,521
-Good work.
-Good job, team.

318
00:14:57,605 --> 00:14:59,607
-I feel so proud.
-Good job.

319
00:14:59,690 --> 00:15:01,609
You made something crazy, didn't you?

320
00:15:01,692 --> 00:15:03,277
-You'll see soon.
-Hey.

321
00:15:03,360 --> 00:15:06,196
BUT WHERE'S THE OWNER?

322
00:15:06,906 --> 00:15:08,240
Almost done.

323
00:15:08,324 --> 00:15:09,867
My creation.

324
00:15:10,743 --> 00:15:14,038
-Hi, we're back.
-You have a good time?

325
00:15:14,121 --> 00:15:16,415
-Yeah.
-How are you? Exhausted?

326
00:15:16,999 --> 00:15:19,335
MEANWHILE DEX PREPARES DINNER

327
00:15:21,003 --> 00:15:23,255
PLENTY OF RICE

328
00:15:28,385 --> 00:15:31,180
Let's start
by chopping the spring cabbage.

329
00:15:31,263 --> 00:15:33,933
-What do you wanna eat?
-Bibimbap.

330
00:15:34,016 --> 00:15:35,392
Spring cabbage bibimbap.

331
00:15:35,476 --> 00:15:38,354
Oh, nice!
I love spring cabbage, let's do it.

332
00:15:38,938 --> 00:15:40,814
LAST DINNER MENU SPRING CABBAGE BIBIMBAP

333
00:15:40,898 --> 00:15:43,067
Hey, Dex, do you need any help?

334
00:15:43,943 --> 00:15:47,112
Nah. Okay, first, we'll cut out the core.

335
00:15:48,197 --> 00:15:49,281
Pop.

336
00:15:50,240 --> 00:15:52,868
Then, we'll remove the dirty leaves.

337
00:15:55,245 --> 00:15:57,039
QUARTER THEM SO THEY'RE EASIER TO EAT

338
00:15:59,625 --> 00:16:00,918
SPRING CABBAGE PREP DONE

339
00:16:01,001 --> 00:16:02,836
Now, for the sauce. Let's see…

340
00:16:02,920 --> 00:16:04,588
MAKING THE SAUCE

341
00:16:11,011 --> 00:16:13,555
ON THE VERGE OF OVERFLOWING

342
00:16:13,639 --> 00:16:15,224
INTO A POT

343
00:16:15,307 --> 00:16:17,309
MEASURING OUT THE SEASONINGS

344
00:16:17,393 --> 00:16:20,479
I'll double the amount, I guess,
since it's a large portion.

345
00:16:20,562 --> 00:16:21,563
HESITATES

346
00:16:23,565 --> 00:16:25,484
TWO TIMES THIS AMOUNT?

347
00:16:26,151 --> 00:16:27,069
AH WHATEVER

348
00:16:27,903 --> 00:16:29,029
LOTS OF RED PEPPER POWDER

349
00:16:30,447 --> 00:16:31,615
LOTS OF MINCED GARLIC TOO

350
00:16:32,700 --> 00:16:34,034
SAND LANCE FISH SAUCE

351
00:16:34,118 --> 00:16:35,202
SOY SAUCE X2

352
00:16:35,285 --> 00:16:36,120
Done.

353
00:16:36,203 --> 00:16:38,163
Then, mix it all together.

354
00:16:38,247 --> 00:16:39,498
It's looking pretty good.

355
00:16:39,581 --> 00:16:41,583
DEX'S GIANT BATCH OF SAUCE IS COMPLETE

356
00:16:45,713 --> 00:16:47,756
THE RICE IS ALSO
ON THE VERGE OF OVERFLOWING

357
00:16:48,549 --> 00:16:49,758
TASTING IN LARGE QUANTITIES TOO

358
00:16:53,262 --> 00:16:54,263
Tastes good.

359
00:16:55,597 --> 00:16:57,182
Perfect rice for bibimbap.

360
00:17:00,269 --> 00:17:03,230
-Need help?
-I'm okay. It's fun, cooking like this.

361
00:17:03,313 --> 00:17:06,025
Hey, are you totally exhausted
by this place?

362
00:17:06,108 --> 00:17:07,985
Did I make it that obvious?

363
00:17:08,569 --> 00:17:09,570
You're not alone.

364
00:17:09,653 --> 00:17:11,071
Well, we're all leaving.

365
00:17:11,155 --> 00:17:13,240
You really helped us out a lot.

366
00:17:13,323 --> 00:17:15,325
Ah, it's my pleasure.

367
00:17:15,409 --> 00:17:17,202
Dex, you'll leave in ten minutes.

368
00:17:17,286 --> 00:17:19,163
Thanks! I'm just finishing up the dinner.

369
00:17:19,872 --> 00:17:21,957
Please don't go.

370
00:17:22,041 --> 00:17:25,586
It's almost done, so why don't I
explain it to you guys till then?

371
00:17:25,669 --> 00:17:27,087
There's plenty of rice.

372
00:17:27,171 --> 00:17:30,507
First, fill it with rice,
put the spring cabbage on top,

373
00:17:30,591 --> 00:17:33,427
and put half a ladle
of this sauce I made on top.

374
00:17:33,510 --> 00:17:34,428
Half a ladle.

375
00:17:34,511 --> 00:17:37,139
Yeah. And then,
the fried eggs are made later.

376
00:17:37,222 --> 00:17:40,350
-You put it on top like this, and done.
-Awesome, thank you.

377
00:17:40,851 --> 00:17:42,478
I'd better get ready to leave now.

378
00:17:42,561 --> 00:17:45,314
-Thanks, man. Have a safe trip.
-I will, and enjoy.

379
00:17:49,359 --> 00:17:51,904
THE PART-TIMER PACKS HIS STUFF

380
00:17:52,821 --> 00:17:54,656
Everyone, I just wanted to say…

381
00:17:54,740 --> 00:17:58,202
I have to go home
after finishing this part-time job, sadly.

382
00:17:58,285 --> 00:17:59,995
WHAT?

383
00:18:00,079 --> 00:18:01,330
ALREADY?

384
00:18:01,413 --> 00:18:02,247
NO!

385
00:18:02,331 --> 00:18:06,502
-You're leaving, just like that?
-Block the door! Don't leave!

386
00:18:06,585 --> 00:18:08,670
If the three of us hold him down,
he can't leave.

387
00:18:08,754 --> 00:18:09,922
Tie him down!

388
00:18:10,005 --> 00:18:13,884
It's hard enough already.
I'm sad to go, but I have to.

389
00:18:13,967 --> 00:18:15,636
-Bye, man. Thanks.
-See you soon.

390
00:18:15,719 --> 00:18:18,013
-Your work is inspiring.
-Bye, guys.

391
00:18:19,098 --> 00:18:20,766
You're gonna have to let go.

392
00:18:21,308 --> 00:18:23,227
-Yeon-koung, Zuha…
-We'll see you soon.

393
00:18:23,310 --> 00:18:26,271
-So great to meet you!
-Wish you could stay longer.

394
00:18:26,355 --> 00:18:28,148
-I'm excited for your dinner.
-You're the best!

395
00:18:28,232 --> 00:18:30,317
-Hope you like the dinner.
-We will.

396
00:18:30,400 --> 00:18:32,861
-On your way out, tell Kian to get back.
-Of course.

397
00:18:32,945 --> 00:18:34,738
-Thanks.
-Close the door?

398
00:18:34,822 --> 00:18:36,615
-Be careful!
-Thanks so much.

399
00:18:36,698 --> 00:18:38,534
I'll miss all of you guys, for sure.

400
00:18:40,035 --> 00:18:42,454
-Heading out? Oh…
-Yeah, I'm out.

401
00:18:43,372 --> 00:18:44,873
-Great work.
-Wow.

402
00:18:44,957 --> 00:18:46,375
SHOCKED

403
00:18:46,458 --> 00:18:48,961
-Does it look scary?
-No, no, no, I think it's cute.

404
00:18:49,044 --> 00:18:51,588
I honestly think it's done.
Wanna go in together?

405
00:18:51,672 --> 00:18:54,800
-Aren't you leaving?
-I have to bring you in.

406
00:18:54,883 --> 00:18:55,759
-Me?
-Yeah.

407
00:18:55,843 --> 00:18:58,095
You can head out. I'm still working.

408
00:18:58,178 --> 00:19:00,472
Well, it looks good.
Everyone wants you to come back.

409
00:19:00,556 --> 00:19:01,640
What do you mean?

410
00:19:01,723 --> 00:19:04,560
-They want to spend time with you.
-Oh…

411
00:19:04,643 --> 00:19:07,896
-The urge to build never ends.
-But you need an intervention.

412
00:19:08,647 --> 00:19:10,774
It looks great. That's enough.

413
00:19:10,858 --> 00:19:12,776
THANKS TO DEX SNOWMAN-BUILDING IS OVER

414
00:19:12,860 --> 00:19:15,362
-Did you have fun?
-I had such a great time.

415
00:19:15,445 --> 00:19:16,613
-For sure.
-That's good.

416
00:19:17,197 --> 00:19:19,616
Since he was constantly
bustling around and working,

417
00:19:19,700 --> 00:19:22,244
it, uh, helped so much
to recharge my energy.

418
00:19:22,327 --> 00:19:25,956
I was grateful that he came to help us.
I really appreciated the support.

419
00:19:26,039 --> 00:19:27,749
-Careful, roads are slippery.
-Will do.

420
00:19:30,752 --> 00:19:31,753
Later, Dex.

421
00:19:32,754 --> 00:19:35,215
You know, both Kian and I, at our age,

422
00:19:35,299 --> 00:19:39,178
it can be hard to find things or people
in life that make you genuinely laugh.

423
00:19:39,261 --> 00:19:42,931
The experience was like a dream.
I think I'll remember it for a long time.

424
00:19:43,015 --> 00:19:45,851
Goodbye, Kian's B&B!

425
00:19:48,395 --> 00:19:50,731
THE PART-TIMER GETS OFF WORK

426
00:19:51,732 --> 00:19:52,816
MEANWHILE, JUN-HO…

427
00:19:53,567 --> 00:19:56,445
Okay, he wants me
to make some fried eggs for the last step.

428
00:19:56,528 --> 00:19:58,238
So each person gets two.

429
00:19:58,906 --> 00:20:00,824
STARTING THE TASK RIGHT AWAY

430
00:20:04,286 --> 00:20:06,121
GOLDEN BROWN

431
00:20:10,125 --> 00:20:11,084
FRIED EGGS COMPLETE

432
00:20:11,168 --> 00:20:13,503
-Okay, all done.
-Did he finish cooking?

433
00:20:13,587 --> 00:20:16,465
-I just did the last bit.
-Let's see. What time is it now?

434
00:20:16,548 --> 00:20:19,468
-Not sure.
-Oh, shit.

435
00:20:19,551 --> 00:20:21,762
I forgot you don't
have your watch. Hey, time?

436
00:20:22,346 --> 00:20:23,972
FLICK

437
00:20:24,056 --> 00:20:24,890
6:12.

438
00:20:24,973 --> 00:20:27,142
-That late? Let's eat.
-Let's serve dinner.

439
00:20:27,226 --> 00:20:30,062
-We should feed everyone.
-Let's get it down.

440
00:20:30,145 --> 00:20:33,106
-You wanna go get it?
-Lower it down to me.

441
00:20:35,400 --> 00:20:36,944
LOWERING THEIR LAST DINNER

442
00:20:37,027 --> 00:20:38,987
-Wow, love it.
-Okay.

443
00:20:39,071 --> 00:20:41,156
-Oh, and the sauce.
-Go slow.

444
00:20:41,823 --> 00:20:43,116
-Rice?
-Hot?

445
00:20:43,200 --> 00:20:45,494
-Hold the handles.
-Okay, thanks.

446
00:20:50,499 --> 00:20:53,835
GROANING

447
00:20:53,919 --> 00:20:54,920
Okay.

448
00:20:56,505 --> 00:20:58,298
-Sesame oil.
-Thanks.

449
00:20:58,382 --> 00:20:59,925
AFTERMATH OF PLAYING IN THE SNOW

450
00:21:00,008 --> 00:21:02,010
-I'm tired.
-Good job, Kian.

451
00:21:02,094 --> 00:21:05,305
-I think we're ready. Shall we?
-Everyone, let's eat.

452
00:21:05,389 --> 00:21:06,974
Would it be all right if we ate outside?

453
00:21:07,057 --> 00:21:08,809
-Of course. It's the perfect evening.
-Okay.

454
00:21:08,892 --> 00:21:11,228
We prepared the tables and chairs for you.

455
00:21:12,271 --> 00:21:14,898
Today, we're lucky
because Dex made dinner.

456
00:21:14,982 --> 00:21:16,900
It's spring cabbage bibimbap.

457
00:21:16,984 --> 00:21:19,861
Put some rice in your bowl
and then spring cabbage on top.

458
00:21:19,945 --> 00:21:23,407
The sauce might be a bit salty,
so just mix in however much you want.

459
00:21:23,490 --> 00:21:25,617
-Dig in.
-Thanks, Dex.

460
00:21:27,577 --> 00:21:30,080
-I'm going easy.
-It may be salty for you.

461
00:21:30,163 --> 00:21:33,083
-Just that much? Have more.
-Okay.

462
00:21:38,839 --> 00:21:40,173
I should use the big bowl.

463
00:21:40,841 --> 00:21:42,551
THE OWNER USES A BIG BOWL

464
00:21:42,634 --> 00:21:45,178
Kian, that bowl matches your personality.

465
00:21:45,262 --> 00:21:47,681
-Yeah? It's less messy.
-Uh-huh.

466
00:21:47,764 --> 00:21:51,184
Grab your coats.
We're going out, dress warm enough.

467
00:21:51,268 --> 00:21:52,102
Okay.

468
00:21:52,185 --> 00:21:54,521
It's super cold outside

469
00:21:54,604 --> 00:21:55,939
THE OWNER'S CHANTING IS CONTAGIOUS

470
00:21:56,023 --> 00:21:59,276
We must put on our jackets
And hats and gloves

471
00:21:59,359 --> 00:22:03,947
To go outside in the snow
Because it's cold as hell

472
00:22:04,614 --> 00:22:07,993
We'll have to be careful
walking down. Don't spill the bibimbap.

473
00:22:09,578 --> 00:22:11,538
-Here we go.
-Follow the owner.

474
00:22:11,621 --> 00:22:12,581
Careful, guys.

475
00:22:12,664 --> 00:22:16,001
We made the stairs
and everything. Head on down.

476
00:22:16,084 --> 00:22:19,379
-You made this? That's so cool! Wow!
-Dex spearheaded the stairs.

477
00:22:19,463 --> 00:22:21,506
Wow. What a creative idea.

478
00:22:21,590 --> 00:22:24,259
I don't think we'd be able
to walk down here without them.

479
00:22:24,343 --> 00:22:26,053
Oh, look at our snowman.

480
00:22:26,136 --> 00:22:28,096
-It's awesome. Who made that?
-Looks good.

481
00:22:28,180 --> 00:22:30,265
Is the one you made on the right or left?

482
00:22:30,349 --> 00:22:33,101
-The left.
-Wow. That's super big.

483
00:22:33,185 --> 00:22:35,354
-Have a seat over there.
-Okay.

484
00:22:36,521 --> 00:22:38,273
PLOPPING DOWN ON THE GROUND

485
00:22:38,357 --> 00:22:39,816
Wait, why did you sit there?

486
00:22:39,900 --> 00:22:42,861
What? Oh, I just wanted you all
to pick your seats first.

487
00:22:43,445 --> 00:22:45,655
Sit, guys. You can sit there, or there.

488
00:22:45,739 --> 00:22:47,449
-That's a chair.
-We'll sit here.

489
00:22:48,533 --> 00:22:50,494
-The chair feels stable, right?
-Yeah, it's great.

490
00:22:50,577 --> 00:22:52,913
We made this.
We really had to pack it together.

491
00:22:52,996 --> 00:22:53,914
EVERYONE IS SEATED

492
00:22:55,540 --> 00:22:56,625
It started snowing.

493
00:22:58,293 --> 00:23:00,295
Wow, so cool. It's magical.

494
00:23:00,379 --> 00:23:02,172
-Yes, so nice.
-Isn't it romantic?

495
00:23:02,255 --> 00:23:04,299
-Yeah.
-All right.

496
00:23:04,383 --> 00:23:06,635
Vibes are even better
now that the sun's down.

497
00:23:06,718 --> 00:23:09,137
-It's insane!
-Absolutely.

498
00:23:09,221 --> 00:23:11,014
When else would we all do this?

499
00:23:11,640 --> 00:23:14,851
Yeah. How is it,
doing this on your birthday, Hyeon-seo?

500
00:23:14,935 --> 00:23:16,895
-This is the best birthday ever.
-It's fun?

501
00:23:16,978 --> 00:23:18,980
-All right, enjoy.
-Enjoy the food.

502
00:23:19,064 --> 00:23:21,066
-This is so cool.
-It's so delicious! Thanks!

503
00:23:21,149 --> 00:23:22,567
Tastes so good.

504
00:23:23,485 --> 00:23:25,654
Mmm…

505
00:23:27,447 --> 00:23:28,698
Pretty good.

506
00:23:29,408 --> 00:23:32,702
-Is it the bibimbap that's trending?
-People eat it all the time now.

507
00:23:34,996 --> 00:23:36,623
A BITE OF SPRING CABBAGE

508
00:23:39,668 --> 00:23:41,294
Is the sauce okay?

509
00:23:41,378 --> 00:23:44,297
I think the sauce made the dish unique.

510
00:23:44,381 --> 00:23:47,801
It wasn't just gochujang.
It had a special savory flavor.

511
00:23:50,595 --> 00:23:51,930
PRECIOUS

512
00:23:52,013 --> 00:23:54,599
I love the smell of the spring cabbage.

513
00:23:54,683 --> 00:23:55,851
I agree.

514
00:23:56,435 --> 00:23:58,437
-Dex did a good job seasoning it.
-He did.

515
00:24:03,692 --> 00:24:05,735
I think I put too much sauce.

516
00:24:06,361 --> 00:24:07,988
A MOMENT AGO

517
00:24:08,071 --> 00:24:09,906
A LOT OF SAUCE

518
00:24:10,490 --> 00:24:11,992
That may be really salty.

519
00:24:12,742 --> 00:24:17,539
-Your rice is red.
-It's not spicy, but, yeah, salty.

520
00:24:18,123 --> 00:24:19,499
Too much salt for you?

521
00:24:19,583 --> 00:24:21,460
Don't suffer.

522
00:24:21,543 --> 00:24:23,170
-Try mixing in snow.
-Huh?

523
00:24:23,253 --> 00:24:26,089
Oh, true. If you add in some snow,
it'll dilute the flavor.

524
00:24:26,173 --> 00:24:28,383
-Uh, okay.
-Seriously?

525
00:24:28,467 --> 00:24:30,886
-Like salt, sprinkle it.
-I guess it won't kill me.

526
00:24:30,969 --> 00:24:33,138
-Try a bit.
-Let's see.

527
00:24:33,722 --> 00:24:34,598
SPRINKLING SNOW

528
00:24:34,681 --> 00:24:37,100
-Are you guys sure?
-Like that, yeah. Now mix it.

529
00:24:42,230 --> 00:24:44,316
Oh! I think it worked.

530
00:24:44,399 --> 00:24:47,152
-Really? Cool.
-For sure. It tastes less salty now.

531
00:24:50,238 --> 00:24:52,782
-Hey, do you want ramyeon?
-Yeah, that'll be nice.

532
00:24:52,866 --> 00:24:55,243
Hey, everyone!
I have ramyeon for you.

533
00:24:55,327 --> 00:24:58,580
-Looks good.
-Looks incredible, thanks.

534
00:24:58,663 --> 00:25:02,667
-It might be a little undercooked.
-I'd never turn down ramyeon.

535
00:25:02,751 --> 00:25:04,127
Wow, yes!

536
00:25:04,211 --> 00:25:06,213
-Oh, enough.
-Okay.

537
00:25:14,721 --> 00:25:16,014
Should I try the soup?

538
00:25:19,267 --> 00:25:20,227
Oh, that's good.

539
00:25:21,394 --> 00:25:22,646
PASSES IT TO THE OWNER

540
00:25:22,729 --> 00:25:23,688
That hits the spot.

541
00:25:27,943 --> 00:25:29,152
Hungry, huh?

542
00:25:29,236 --> 00:25:30,320
AHHHH

543
00:25:31,863 --> 00:25:34,616
-His whole face is covered.
-That warmed my stomach so well.

544
00:25:38,912 --> 00:25:39,913
Ah, that's killer.

545
00:25:39,996 --> 00:25:42,874
-I'm glad we did this. It's nice for them.
-Yeah. Love it.

546
00:25:42,958 --> 00:25:44,626
-It's a nice vibe here.
-Exactly.

547
00:25:44,709 --> 00:25:48,630
-Look at everyone sitting together.
-Talking, having fun.

548
00:25:48,713 --> 00:25:53,343
We really wanted to make this vision
a reality. And we really did it. Wow.

549
00:25:53,426 --> 00:25:54,803
We did good.

550
00:25:54,886 --> 00:25:56,179
Good vibes.

551
00:25:56,263 --> 00:25:57,264
Good vibes.

552
00:25:57,347 --> 00:25:59,933
We love good vibes.

553
00:26:00,016 --> 00:26:01,393
Today is good vibes.

554
00:26:01,476 --> 00:26:02,686
AFTER A DINNER WITH NICE VIBES

555
00:26:02,769 --> 00:26:05,313
Everyone, feel free to go inside
whenever you want.

556
00:26:05,397 --> 00:26:07,065
I'll wash those first.

557
00:26:07,148 --> 00:26:08,692
YEON-KOUNG, ZUHA IN CHARGE OF THE DISHES

558
00:26:18,201 --> 00:26:19,244
We, uh…

559
00:26:19,327 --> 00:26:20,161
WE?

560
00:26:20,245 --> 00:26:21,871
…just had our last meal.

561
00:26:21,955 --> 00:26:23,290
It's crazy.

562
00:26:23,373 --> 00:26:24,833
-Oh, wow.
-The final one.

563
00:26:25,584 --> 00:26:27,794
We really worked our butts off, didn't we?

564
00:26:28,837 --> 00:26:31,715
-Could you toss that out?
-Yeah.

565
00:26:31,798 --> 00:26:33,717
CLEANING UP THE LEFTOVERS

566
00:26:35,051 --> 00:26:36,052
There's a lot.

567
00:26:37,470 --> 00:26:39,681
A LOT OF FOOD WASTE PILED UP

568
00:26:40,890 --> 00:26:42,684
-Grab the food waste?
-Okay.

569
00:26:43,268 --> 00:26:47,105
-We're gonna put it in the storage shed.
-But tie it up beforehand.

570
00:26:47,814 --> 00:26:48,815
There's a lot.

571
00:26:54,154 --> 00:26:56,114
HEAVY

572
00:26:56,990 --> 00:26:58,742
How should we get this down there?

573
00:27:00,744 --> 00:27:02,829
What? No!

574
00:27:02,912 --> 00:27:06,249
What? No! No!

575
00:27:09,628 --> 00:27:11,504
-No!
-No!

576
00:27:11,588 --> 00:27:12,756
-I can't…
-This sucks!

577
00:27:12,839 --> 00:27:14,299
It's awful!

578
00:27:14,883 --> 00:27:16,593
It's awful!

579
00:27:17,510 --> 00:27:19,679
-No, no, no!
-No!

580
00:27:26,269 --> 00:27:27,228
What? What? What?

581
00:27:27,312 --> 00:27:28,938
WHAT'S GOING ON?

582
00:27:29,022 --> 00:27:30,649
-The bag broke.
-It burst.

583
00:27:32,901 --> 00:27:34,819
Why? Oh, the smell.

584
00:27:34,903 --> 00:27:35,862
Ah, the smell!

585
00:27:35,945 --> 00:27:37,572
SOME GOT ON HIS FOOT

586
00:27:37,656 --> 00:27:39,574
A HOT MESS

587
00:27:40,075 --> 00:27:42,077
-Hold on a sec.
-What do we do?

588
00:27:42,827 --> 00:27:46,039
-Let's see what we can do.
-You messed up big time.

589
00:27:46,122 --> 00:27:47,832
LIMPING

590
00:27:48,416 --> 00:27:50,043
Hold on. I need to wipe my feet off.

591
00:27:50,126 --> 00:27:52,045
-Give me that.
-Go, go, go.

592
00:27:52,128 --> 00:27:53,505
Yuck.

593
00:27:56,549 --> 00:27:59,219
Something was rotten in there.

594
00:27:59,302 --> 00:28:01,721
Well, at least,
it didn't explode on my head.

595
00:28:03,181 --> 00:28:06,267
-Let's figure out what to do.
-Man. What are we gonna do about the mess?

596
00:28:06,351 --> 00:28:08,228
Here, let me try.

597
00:28:10,313 --> 00:28:11,690
Oh, it's inside the cracks.

598
00:28:15,276 --> 00:28:16,319
SNIFF
SNIFF

599
00:28:16,403 --> 00:28:19,572
WOOZY

600
00:28:22,742 --> 00:28:23,618
A NEW PLASTIC BAG

601
00:28:30,166 --> 00:28:32,627
-I'll go down and grab it from you.
-Let's be careful.

602
00:28:34,838 --> 00:28:35,839
Okay.

603
00:28:38,049 --> 00:28:39,217
Okay. Yes!

604
00:28:39,300 --> 00:28:40,885
TRANSPORTING IT DOWN SAFELY

605
00:28:43,054 --> 00:28:44,013
Gross.

606
00:28:45,849 --> 00:28:47,517
WHILE THEY CLEAN UP THE FOOD WASTE

607
00:28:47,600 --> 00:28:48,643
-Zip, zap.
-Zap.

608
00:28:48,727 --> 00:28:50,103
-Zop!
-Zip, zap!

609
00:28:50,186 --> 00:28:51,312
-Zop!
-Zip!

610
00:28:51,396 --> 00:28:52,605
-Zap.
-Zop.

611
00:28:52,689 --> 00:28:53,982
-Zip!
-Zap. Zip!

612
00:28:54,065 --> 00:28:55,066
-Zap!
-Zop!

613
00:28:55,150 --> 00:28:56,067
Zop!

614
00:28:57,485 --> 00:29:00,155
THE OLDER MALES ARE EXCITED
ABOUT THE YOUNGER MALES' PUNISHMENT

615
00:29:00,238 --> 00:29:01,531
Wanna do "Tell me"?

616
00:29:04,784 --> 00:29:06,870
-Where are you starting?
-No music?

617
00:29:06,953 --> 00:29:08,121
SHY

618
00:29:08,204 --> 00:29:09,205
Now you guess.

619
00:29:09,289 --> 00:29:10,665
-Two?
-Three?

620
00:29:10,749 --> 00:29:12,876
-The kids are getting along.
-They love each other.

621
00:29:12,959 --> 00:29:15,128
Let's clean up the kitchen a bit,
close it up for good.

622
00:29:15,211 --> 00:29:17,130
-The whole thing?
-Yep.

623
00:29:17,756 --> 00:29:19,299
ORGANIZING THE SEASONINGS

624
00:29:21,801 --> 00:29:22,761
All right.

625
00:29:22,844 --> 00:29:24,304
LINED UP PERFECTLY

626
00:29:26,473 --> 00:29:28,725
THE OWNER PUTS AWAY THE CLEAN DISHES

627
00:29:28,808 --> 00:29:30,810
Oh, man. Literally, all we do is clean.

628
00:29:30,894 --> 00:29:32,896
-Goodness gracious.
-Man.

629
00:29:32,979 --> 00:29:35,064
-We're in the home stretch.
-Man, oh, man.

630
00:29:35,148 --> 00:29:36,691
-Come on!
-Oh, man.

631
00:29:39,027 --> 00:29:40,153
Can we stop now?

632
00:29:40,737 --> 00:29:42,989
-Looks good to me.
-It's clean enough, right?

633
00:29:45,116 --> 00:29:47,744
KNOCKED OUT

634
00:29:50,622 --> 00:29:53,416
Oh, I'm so exhausted,
I don't know if I can move.

635
00:29:53,500 --> 00:29:54,459
WORN OUT

636
00:29:56,252 --> 00:29:57,212
THE DISHES ARE DONE

637
00:29:57,295 --> 00:29:58,922
-All done.
-We did it.

638
00:30:01,049 --> 00:30:02,175
All right, we're done.

639
00:30:04,803 --> 00:30:06,054
Great job, guys.

640
00:30:07,096 --> 00:30:10,266
Isn't it kinda crazy to think
we'll be officially closed tomorrow?

641
00:30:10,350 --> 00:30:13,144
-Especially for you, as the owner.
-Of course.

642
00:30:13,728 --> 00:30:14,979
Yeah, it's bittersweet.

643
00:30:21,569 --> 00:30:22,779
But, boss, you know what?

644
00:30:24,405 --> 00:30:27,492
-Today is not even close to being over.
-I know I have to be grateful for it all.

645
00:30:27,575 --> 00:30:30,119
-It's not over.
-The night is just getting started!

646
00:30:31,037 --> 00:30:34,499
-It's just getting started.
-We'll party all night long.

647
00:30:34,582 --> 00:30:37,335
We're gonna have a great night.
Let's focus on that right now.

648
00:30:39,379 --> 00:30:41,214
Oh, man, screw this.

649
00:30:45,802 --> 00:30:47,887
This is so freaking exhausting.

650
00:30:49,514 --> 00:30:51,683
This is so freaking exhausting.

651
00:30:52,433 --> 00:30:54,686
He's right.

652
00:30:55,311 --> 00:30:57,188
I think there's a good chance I might die.

653
00:30:57,272 --> 00:30:58,356
HIS TRUE FEELINGS SLIP OUT

654
00:30:58,940 --> 00:31:00,859
Let it all out, Kian.

655
00:31:01,776 --> 00:31:04,153
Hang in there a little longer.
It's almost over.

656
00:31:04,654 --> 00:31:06,114
8:00 P.M.

657
00:31:06,197 --> 00:31:07,949
I've been really eager to ask you.

658
00:31:08,032 --> 00:31:11,703
How much do you practice every day
for your gaming?

659
00:31:11,786 --> 00:31:13,288
On average, about 12 hours.

660
00:31:13,371 --> 00:31:15,331
-Twelve hours?!
-Oh, yeah. Just about.

661
00:31:15,415 --> 00:31:19,711
Isn't that a lot, though? For one day?
What time do you start in the morning?

662
00:31:19,794 --> 00:31:22,130
-We usually start at 1:00 p.m.
-You start that late?

663
00:31:22,213 --> 00:31:26,009
Yeah. So we start playing team games
from 1:00 to 4:00 p.m.

664
00:31:26,092 --> 00:31:28,970
And then, we play team games
from 7:00 to 10:00 p.m.

665
00:31:29,637 --> 00:31:33,057
And after 11:00 p.m.,
we will start our individual practice.

666
00:31:33,141 --> 00:31:35,894
-You play till late, is that right?
-We do.

667
00:31:35,977 --> 00:31:37,896
We go to bed around 4:00 or 5:00
in the morning.

668
00:31:38,479 --> 00:31:40,815
So you really do practice
for the majority of your day.

669
00:31:40,899 --> 00:31:42,150
That's right.

670
00:31:42,233 --> 00:31:44,652
-Yeon-koung, can I ask you a question?
-Yeah.

671
00:31:45,945 --> 00:31:49,449
How have you coped with slumps
in your career? If you've had them.

672
00:31:49,532 --> 00:31:51,367
Oh, I've definitely had slumps.

673
00:31:51,451 --> 00:31:54,537
When I was in my late twenties,

674
00:31:54,621 --> 00:31:58,041
I went through a pretty intense slump.
I assume you started young?

675
00:31:58,124 --> 00:32:00,793
-Since I was young.
-You're still young.

676
00:32:01,377 --> 00:32:04,380
I started playing volleyball
when I was in fourth grade.

677
00:32:04,464 --> 00:32:07,467
I was thrilled when I was selected
as a national team player.

678
00:32:08,176 --> 00:32:10,219
But I started playing as a kid
because I liked it.

679
00:32:10,303 --> 00:32:12,263
But once I started to feel the pressure

680
00:32:12,347 --> 00:32:14,682
and it started to feel like a job,
it changed.

681
00:32:14,766 --> 00:32:16,809
I lost the fun and fell into a slump.

682
00:32:16,893 --> 00:32:19,562
-Oh…
-Like, "What am I doing?"

683
00:32:20,229 --> 00:32:22,065
Like, "What?"

684
00:32:22,148 --> 00:32:25,526
I was just going through the motions
at some point, you know?

685
00:32:25,610 --> 00:32:27,403
Things can feel stagnant sometimes.

686
00:32:27,487 --> 00:32:31,240
Yeah, I was so used to it all
that I forgot about so many of the things

687
00:32:31,324 --> 00:32:32,784
that were important to me.

688
00:32:33,409 --> 00:32:37,538
So whenever I go through something
like that where I lose track of myself,

689
00:32:37,622 --> 00:32:39,958
I try to remember
why I started playing to begin with

690
00:32:40,041 --> 00:32:41,793
and to feel that kind of joy again.

691
00:32:42,377 --> 00:32:45,755
T1 is a really successful organization.
You guys are big, right?

692
00:32:45,838 --> 00:32:47,298
-Yeah.
-The resolve you needed

693
00:32:47,382 --> 00:32:49,092
when you first joined the team…

694
00:32:50,051 --> 00:32:52,220
-There was a fire you had in you.
-For sure.

695
00:32:52,303 --> 00:32:53,930
So maybe when things are feeling stale,

696
00:32:54,013 --> 00:32:56,474
you can think back to that person
you were before

697
00:32:56,557 --> 00:32:59,435
and how much you wanted to be
where you are now, you know?

698
00:33:00,687 --> 00:33:02,605
-Most importantly, don't forget.
-Yeah.

699
00:33:02,689 --> 00:33:05,066
-We started this because we like it.
-You're right.

700
00:33:05,149 --> 00:33:07,026
-Our passion led us where we are.
-Passion, yeah.

701
00:33:07,110 --> 00:33:09,570
And it still lives inside us.
That's why we do what we do.

702
00:33:10,279 --> 00:33:11,948
-That's really well said.
-Yeah?

703
00:33:12,907 --> 00:33:15,785
-Maybe I should start watching you play.
-Oh, really?

704
00:33:15,868 --> 00:33:18,705
-I'll be rooting for T1.
-Oh, yes, please. Always.

705
00:33:18,788 --> 00:33:22,166
Oh, my God. We have to make the cake now.

706
00:33:26,421 --> 00:33:27,338
Okay, so…

707
00:33:27,422 --> 00:33:28,381
WHERE IS HYEON-SEO?

708
00:33:28,464 --> 00:33:30,383
RUSTLING

709
00:33:30,466 --> 00:33:33,761
Today's Hyeon-seo's birthday,
so I wanted to make him a cake.

710
00:33:33,845 --> 00:33:34,804
WITHOUT HIM KNOWING

711
00:33:34,887 --> 00:33:35,930
-Cookies?
-Margaret?

712
00:33:36,014 --> 00:33:37,640
We can add those.

713
00:33:38,224 --> 00:33:40,643
-I think it's perfect.
-It's nice, right?

714
00:33:41,227 --> 00:33:43,062
That's happening right now?

715
00:33:43,146 --> 00:33:44,647
Live broadcast from Seoul.

716
00:33:44,731 --> 00:33:45,690
TOTAL LUNAR ECLIPSE

717
00:33:45,773 --> 00:33:47,525
-We can't see it from here?
-No.

718
00:33:47,608 --> 00:33:49,068
I want to see it for real.

719
00:33:49,152 --> 00:33:50,653
At least we can watch it here.

720
00:33:51,362 --> 00:33:56,034
So, when the moon turns completely red,
that means that it's, you know, aligned?

721
00:33:56,117 --> 00:33:58,077
Yes, and that'll be at 8:30.

722
00:33:58,161 --> 00:33:59,120
BLOOD MOON

723
00:33:59,203 --> 00:34:01,497
EARTH'S SHADOW COVERS THE MOON
AND MAKES IT GLOW RED

724
00:34:01,581 --> 00:34:04,125
-We can all watch.
-We have experts here.

725
00:34:04,208 --> 00:34:05,960
-Blood moon.
-Oh, look.

726
00:34:06,044 --> 00:34:07,295
Should we make a wish?

727
00:34:07,378 --> 00:34:09,338
-You want to make a wish?
-We should, yeah.

728
00:34:09,422 --> 00:34:11,466
-It's a cosmic event.
-So we each get a wish.

729
00:34:11,549 --> 00:34:12,675
Okay, ready?

730
00:34:12,759 --> 00:34:15,428
-What the hell?
-Come make a wish.

731
00:34:16,137 --> 00:34:17,180
Yeah, but hurry up.

732
00:34:18,056 --> 00:34:19,265
KNEELING DOWN

733
00:34:20,224 --> 00:34:22,393
-Come make a wish on a blood moon.
-What are you doing?

734
00:34:22,477 --> 00:34:23,811
-Zuha, come here.
-We're praying.

735
00:34:23,895 --> 00:34:25,354
-Praying? Okay.
-The eclipse started.

736
00:34:25,938 --> 00:34:28,357
Let these guys get into good universities.

737
00:34:28,441 --> 00:34:30,109
PRAYING FOR THE HIGH SCHOOLERS

738
00:34:33,613 --> 00:34:36,074
All right, we have another thing planned.
Let's go outside.

739
00:34:37,241 --> 00:34:39,202
-Should we go?
-Outside.

740
00:34:39,285 --> 00:34:41,621
-Let's go first.
-I'll lead. Let's beat them out there.

741
00:34:42,205 --> 00:34:44,082
JUN-HO GOES AHEAD WITH THE CAKE

742
00:34:44,165 --> 00:34:45,666
Let's hide it behind here.

743
00:34:48,127 --> 00:34:49,670
HE HIDES THE CAKE

744
00:34:49,754 --> 00:34:51,714
We're going outside a lot today.

745
00:34:51,798 --> 00:34:53,633
-The chairs. Take a seat.
-Okay.

746
00:34:53,716 --> 00:34:55,468
SITTING DOWN

747
00:34:55,551 --> 00:34:56,928
-Let's sit.
-Okay.

748
00:34:57,011 --> 00:34:59,555
Come get one of these each. There you go.

749
00:34:59,639 --> 00:35:02,558
Let's light candles and have a moment
for people to share their feelings.

750
00:35:02,642 --> 00:35:03,935
Yeah, try to keep it lit.

751
00:35:06,521 --> 00:35:07,522
That's it.

752
00:35:10,233 --> 00:35:11,818
-Think everyone has one.
-Need yours lit?

753
00:35:11,901 --> 00:35:13,903
-Are all of them lit?
-Yes.

754
00:35:14,487 --> 00:35:15,738
Careful, everyone.

755
00:35:17,198 --> 00:35:19,575
-Can you see any stars?
-No, but we might still.

756
00:35:19,659 --> 00:35:21,452
Hyeon-seo, give me yours.

757
00:35:23,663 --> 00:35:25,206
I'll take that.

758
00:35:25,289 --> 00:35:26,332
But why?

759
00:35:27,750 --> 00:35:29,752
VERY SUSPICIOUS

760
00:35:29,836 --> 00:35:32,255
-Huh?
-For Hyeon-seo.

761
00:35:32,338 --> 00:35:34,090
It's his birthday today.

762
00:35:34,674 --> 00:35:35,675
Yeah.

763
00:35:36,259 --> 00:35:39,387
-So instead of birthday candles…
-Uh-huh!

764
00:35:40,096 --> 00:35:41,764
And one, two, three.

765
00:35:41,848 --> 00:35:47,395
Happy birthday to you
Happy birthday to you

766
00:35:47,478 --> 00:35:53,818
Happy birthday, dear Hyeon-seo
Happy birthday to you

767
00:35:53,901 --> 00:35:55,319
Happy birthday!

768
00:35:59,782 --> 00:36:01,200
-Happy birthday!
-Thank you!

769
00:36:01,284 --> 00:36:02,869
-Happy birthday.
-Please dig in.

770
00:36:02,952 --> 00:36:04,704
-You should have all of it.
-That's your cake.

771
00:36:05,705 --> 00:36:06,998
-Happy birthday.
-Cheers!

772
00:36:07,081 --> 00:36:10,084
Everyone, tonight is unfortunately
our final night.

773
00:36:11,752 --> 00:36:14,213
And tonight, there's…
What is it, a red moon?

774
00:36:14,297 --> 00:36:18,092
We're going to pretend we can see it
and make a wish.

775
00:36:18,176 --> 00:36:21,512
So, for my wish,
it actually came true on this trip.

776
00:36:21,596 --> 00:36:23,306
It was to meet Ms. Kim Yeon-koung.

777
00:36:24,891 --> 00:36:27,768
So my wish for tonight is to pass
my teacher certification exams.

778
00:36:27,852 --> 00:36:29,312
-You can do it.
-Good luck.

779
00:36:29,395 --> 00:36:31,105
-All right.
-Thank you.

780
00:36:31,189 --> 00:36:32,607
Ice climbing is a niche sport,

781
00:36:32,690 --> 00:36:35,359
but there's rumors we may be
included someday in the Olympics.

782
00:36:35,443 --> 00:36:36,652
Nice.

783
00:36:36,736 --> 00:36:39,113
So my wish is for us to be
at the Olympics in 2030.

784
00:36:39,197 --> 00:36:41,282
And I think you will. Yeah.

785
00:36:41,866 --> 00:36:44,660
My goal is to become the world champion
in ice climbing.

786
00:36:44,744 --> 00:36:47,705
-You'll have to take Young-geon's place.
-Sure, he can try.

787
00:36:47,788 --> 00:36:50,666
-At least I'll give it a shot.
-You guys can be friendly rivals.

788
00:36:50,750 --> 00:36:52,168
-Good one.
-Best of luck.

789
00:36:52,251 --> 00:36:56,047
We have a League of Legends championship,
and we've won three years in a row.

790
00:36:56,130 --> 00:36:58,299
I'm really hoping
we can win our fourth this year.

791
00:36:58,382 --> 00:36:59,717
That's cool.

792
00:36:59,800 --> 00:37:01,636
That's our goal,
we'll work hard to achieve it.

793
00:37:01,719 --> 00:37:04,055
Yeah, I know you got this.

794
00:37:04,138 --> 00:37:07,892
When you're stressed or sad,
looking up at the night sky can help.

795
00:37:07,975 --> 00:37:09,268
That's why it's amazing.

796
00:37:09,352 --> 00:37:13,606
And I hope you all can do that
and have fun lives. Thank you.

797
00:37:15,775 --> 00:37:19,320
First, I'd like to share
something I've been thinking about.

798
00:37:19,403 --> 00:37:21,822
So I've been doing what I do
for a super duper long time.

799
00:37:21,906 --> 00:37:25,117
I've also experienced my fair share
of slumps and frustrations.

800
00:37:25,910 --> 00:37:29,038
But I'm so moved by everyone's
different stories and passions.

801
00:37:29,121 --> 00:37:31,832
Through getting to know you,
I'm leaving here inspired.

802
00:37:31,916 --> 00:37:33,918
And I hope you know
that we're rooting for you.

803
00:37:34,001 --> 00:37:35,670
We wish you health and happiness.

804
00:37:36,921 --> 00:37:38,256
-That's so kind.
-Thank you.

805
00:37:38,339 --> 00:37:40,341
I think I'm still trying to grow,

806
00:37:40,424 --> 00:37:43,636
and I'm in the process of becoming
a better version of myself every day.

807
00:37:44,470 --> 00:37:48,432
So my wish is for support on my journey
as I try to be the best person I can be.

808
00:37:50,601 --> 00:37:54,855
Yes, hello. I'm Kim Yeon-koung.
Yes, you all know me.

809
00:37:54,939 --> 00:37:57,275
After what felt like a lifetime last year,

810
00:37:57,358 --> 00:38:00,152
I finally retired from being
a professional volleyball player.

811
00:38:00,236 --> 00:38:02,196
And I spent a lot of my time since,

812
00:38:02,280 --> 00:38:05,491
trying to figure out what I wanted to do
in my life and who I am

813
00:38:05,574 --> 00:38:06,659
if I'm no longer an athlete.

814
00:38:06,742 --> 00:38:10,496
And it's a big decision,
but I came to Kian's B&B

815
00:38:10,579 --> 00:38:12,915
and I met a ton of people
from different walks of life

816
00:38:12,999 --> 00:38:15,209
and listened to a lot of stories.

817
00:38:15,293 --> 00:38:17,795
And it allowed me to learn,
organize my thoughts,

818
00:38:17,878 --> 00:38:20,548
and you all gave me some perspective
outside of my life, so…

819
00:38:22,925 --> 00:38:24,927
Since the boss told me to share something,

820
00:38:25,011 --> 00:38:28,723
my wish is to find something
that makes my heart race this year.

821
00:38:28,806 --> 00:38:31,976
Something that feels like how volleyball
felt when I first started to play.

822
00:38:32,059 --> 00:38:33,728
So even if I don't find it this year,

823
00:38:33,811 --> 00:38:37,315
now I know I want to keep looking
and keep discovering until I find it.

824
00:38:37,398 --> 00:38:40,067
Whether I work in sports
or somewhere else,

825
00:38:40,151 --> 00:38:44,488
I'll be passionate about it, approach it
with the same tenacity as sports and B&Bs.

826
00:38:44,572 --> 00:38:46,240
Thank you all. Thanks.

827
00:38:53,205 --> 00:38:56,167
-I feel like I'm going to cry.
-That's okay. You can.

828
00:38:56,250 --> 00:38:59,086
I got a little emotional right there.
Oh, I feel…

829
00:39:00,212 --> 00:39:01,464
I'm going to cry, guys.

830
00:39:03,049 --> 00:39:04,342
Thank you all for sharing.

831
00:39:04,425 --> 00:39:07,720
And I want to say, growing up,
I was never class president.

832
00:39:07,803 --> 00:39:10,639
And I always felt my skills
as a leader were lacking.

833
00:39:10,723 --> 00:39:13,225
But when we're here,
I feel motivated to do better.

834
00:39:14,018 --> 00:39:17,063
-Was everything okay for you guys?
-Yes, it was awesome.

835
00:39:17,146 --> 00:39:18,189
It was all right.

836
00:39:19,899 --> 00:39:22,526
Well, I hope that
all your wishes come true

837
00:39:22,610 --> 00:39:25,863
and that you never let a little snow
put out your fire for life.

838
00:39:25,946 --> 00:39:28,282
And we have one last event for you now,

839
00:39:28,366 --> 00:39:30,034
-if you'll follow me this way.
-What is it?

840
00:39:30,951 --> 00:39:32,078
What are you doing?

841
00:39:32,161 --> 00:39:35,206
And go ahead
and blow out your candles. All right.

842
00:39:35,956 --> 00:39:37,041
Oh, wow.

843
00:39:38,584 --> 00:39:41,212
-What's it gonna be?
-So much suspense.

844
00:39:41,295 --> 00:39:45,299
Okay, to everyone who came to Kian's B&B
and to everyone who's been here,

845
00:39:45,383 --> 00:39:49,011
not just today, I hope all your wishes
and dreams come true.

846
00:39:49,095 --> 00:39:50,679
So we've prepared…

847
00:39:50,763 --> 00:39:52,723
-this little button for you.
-Huh?

848
00:39:52,807 --> 00:39:53,933
-What?
-A button?

849
00:39:56,394 --> 00:39:57,978
Oh, my God. It's big.

850
00:39:59,105 --> 00:40:00,189
A button.

851
00:40:00,272 --> 00:40:01,315
A HUGE BUTTON

852
00:40:01,399 --> 00:40:03,317
-Cool.
-We prepared an event

853
00:40:03,401 --> 00:40:07,780
where all of you will press this button
and it'll work its magic on you.

854
00:40:08,280 --> 00:40:11,700
So, uh, yeah,
your wishes get bigger and, uh…

855
00:40:13,035 --> 00:40:15,913
Would you all like to press this button
at the same time?

856
00:40:15,996 --> 00:40:19,458
-Yeah!
-Yeah? All right. One, two, three.

857
00:40:24,004 --> 00:40:26,382
What happened?

858
00:40:37,226 --> 00:40:40,688
FIREWORKS EXPLODE
OVER THE WHITE FIELD OF SNOW

859
00:40:44,525 --> 00:40:45,943
That looks incredible!

860
00:40:57,746 --> 00:41:00,875
I always wanted to have fireworks
on the last day, like we did in Season 1.

861
00:41:00,958 --> 00:41:03,502
But if we just set them off,
it would've been like,

862
00:41:03,586 --> 00:41:05,212
"Hey, enjoy the fireworks." That's it.

863
00:41:05,296 --> 00:41:08,966
I wanted to make it feel like their wishes
were growing bigger and brighter,

864
00:41:09,049 --> 00:41:10,050
just like the fireworks.

865
00:41:10,134 --> 00:41:11,969
In Season 1, I pressed the button alone,

866
00:41:12,052 --> 00:41:14,430
but I wanted everyone
to do it together this time.

867
00:41:14,513 --> 00:41:15,598
A BUTTON TO PUSH TOGETHER

868
00:41:18,726 --> 00:41:20,227
They're so pretty.

869
00:41:23,731 --> 00:41:27,067
I probably won't ever get to experience
something like this again. It was so nice.

870
00:41:29,320 --> 00:41:32,573
They were fireworks that would make
all our wishes come true.

871
00:41:32,656 --> 00:41:34,950
It was a fantastic, romantic surprise.

872
00:41:36,202 --> 00:41:37,453
It was so touching,

873
00:41:37,536 --> 00:41:40,664
and I thought that was such
an amazing vision the boss had.

874
00:41:41,457 --> 00:41:44,335
We're so close to them.
This is once-in-a-lifetime.

875
00:41:44,418 --> 00:41:46,086
It was really special.

876
00:41:46,170 --> 00:41:48,797
It reminded me of something
you'd see in a movie.

877
00:41:48,881 --> 00:41:51,383
It was a nice gift
that helped us wrap up our trip

878
00:41:51,467 --> 00:41:53,886
that was short and sweet, like a dream.

879
00:42:12,071 --> 00:42:14,073
-Thank you so much!
-Best fireworks ever.

880
00:42:14,156 --> 00:42:16,909
-Man, that was amazing!
-Such a magical vibe.

881
00:42:19,245 --> 00:42:21,247
ONE MORE TIME

882
00:42:21,330 --> 00:42:22,456
One more time.

883
00:42:22,998 --> 00:42:23,999
Let's push it.

884
00:42:24,708 --> 00:42:26,001
PUSHING IT AGAIN

885
00:42:26,085 --> 00:42:29,171
Sorry, we can only press it once.
The budget's not that big.

886
00:42:29,838 --> 00:42:31,215
Guess we have to recycle this too.

887
00:42:32,508 --> 00:42:34,843
I can't believe
we saw fireworks that close.

888
00:42:36,262 --> 00:42:38,514
Oh, shit.

889
00:42:41,517 --> 00:42:44,019
Boss, I'll miss your slapstick comedy.

890
00:42:44,603 --> 00:42:46,772
-That was a great surprise.
-Good.

891
00:42:46,855 --> 00:42:48,607
-Best night ever.
-I'll remember it.

892
00:42:50,609 --> 00:42:53,153
With that, everything we prepared is over.

893
00:42:53,237 --> 00:42:55,406
-It was amazing.
-What did you think?

894
00:42:55,489 --> 00:42:57,908
-Everyone loved it so much. Yeah.
-Really?

895
00:42:57,992 --> 00:43:00,244
It wasn't much,
but I tried to make it as cool as I could.

896
00:43:00,327 --> 00:43:01,453
It was cool.

897
00:43:01,537 --> 00:43:04,707
When else in life are we going to see
fireworks that close and over the snow?

898
00:43:08,544 --> 00:43:09,962
-They were a big hit.
-Yeah?

899
00:43:10,045 --> 00:43:12,506
And it was nice
that we pressed the button together.

900
00:43:12,590 --> 00:43:15,426
It felt like we were all doing
something meaningful together.

901
00:43:16,176 --> 00:43:18,387
Is it cool that I'm turning off
half the lights?

902
00:43:18,470 --> 00:43:20,306
9:30 P.M.

903
00:43:20,389 --> 00:43:22,558
THEY TALK IN SMALL GROUPS

904
00:43:23,225 --> 00:43:25,436
That's really great, like,
the fact that people

905
00:43:25,519 --> 00:43:27,855
who are close to each other
can still compete

906
00:43:27,938 --> 00:43:30,232
-with maturity and respect.
-And they cheer each other on.

907
00:43:30,316 --> 00:43:32,109
Yeah, the fact that
you can do that naturally.

908
00:43:32,192 --> 00:43:33,485
How is that even possible?

909
00:43:33,569 --> 00:43:36,530
It's human nature to feel jealous,
even if it's your friend.

910
00:43:36,614 --> 00:43:37,615
That makes sense.

911
00:43:38,532 --> 00:43:40,743
But you guys compete
in a really healthy way.

912
00:43:40,826 --> 00:43:43,370
-Yeah.
-That perspective is refreshing.

913
00:43:43,954 --> 00:43:48,334
To be honest, I didn't know there were
this many lesser-known sports out there,

914
00:43:48,417 --> 00:43:50,502
-like luge, ice climbing.
-Same.

915
00:43:50,586 --> 00:43:51,587
-That's common.
-Yeah.

916
00:43:51,670 --> 00:43:55,382
It's amazing that you're representing
our country as the best in the world.

917
00:43:56,008 --> 00:43:57,092
Even without support.

918
00:43:57,176 --> 00:44:01,180
Even if we try to promote ourselves,
it's such a lesser-known sport.

919
00:44:01,263 --> 00:44:04,224
And the infrastructure is so small,
there's no support.

920
00:44:04,308 --> 00:44:07,311
It's just tricky because
we're doing everything ourselves.

921
00:44:07,394 --> 00:44:10,981
We try to do everything at once,
train, advocate for ourselves.

922
00:44:11,065 --> 00:44:14,652
Then again,
if it does become an Olympic event,

923
00:44:14,735 --> 00:44:17,404
we're hoping it opens
a lot of opportunities for the sport.

924
00:44:17,488 --> 00:44:18,989
That makes a lot of sense.

925
00:44:19,073 --> 00:44:21,241
That's why it's such an important goal.

926
00:44:22,368 --> 00:44:23,494
I know how you feel.

927
00:44:23,577 --> 00:44:25,663
I was so frustrated
when I was playing overseas.

928
00:44:25,746 --> 00:44:28,415
-I was playing in Türkiye then.
-I haven't heard this story.

929
00:44:28,499 --> 00:44:30,918
Back then,
I was sort of at the top of my game.

930
00:44:31,001 --> 00:44:32,544
I was dominating everyone,

931
00:44:32,628 --> 00:44:34,713
but because volleyball
isn't a popular sport,

932
00:44:34,797 --> 00:44:36,006
I didn't get any press at all.

933
00:44:36,090 --> 00:44:38,926
I was a top scorer,
but I didn't get any attention.

934
00:44:39,009 --> 00:44:40,636
I felt unsupported during that time.

935
00:44:41,220 --> 00:44:44,723
But luckily, after I went to the Olympics,
I got some recognition.

936
00:44:44,807 --> 00:44:46,934
-But you're not getting that opportunity.
-That's right.

937
00:44:47,017 --> 00:44:48,268
It's unfortunate.

938
00:44:51,230 --> 00:44:55,442
As an athlete, I know how it feels
to be in an unpopular sport.

939
00:44:56,110 --> 00:44:57,486
You're working so hard,

940
00:44:57,569 --> 00:44:59,863
but no matter how well you do,
you still get passed over.

941
00:44:59,947 --> 00:45:02,157
So I had a lot of empathy for their story.

942
00:45:02,241 --> 00:45:04,576
They had to pay their own expenses,
even when they were going

943
00:45:04,660 --> 00:45:06,787
to the world championships,
which they won.

944
00:45:06,870 --> 00:45:08,288
It made me think about…

945
00:45:08,956 --> 00:45:12,459
how much they've had to sacrifice
and what a toll that must have taken.

946
00:45:13,210 --> 00:45:14,670
I found that heart-wrenching.

947
00:45:15,337 --> 00:45:17,840
These guys are so hardworking
and talented.

948
00:45:18,799 --> 00:45:21,301
I'm positive that good things
are coming their way.

949
00:45:21,385 --> 00:45:24,847
-And maybe the Olympics.
-Yeah. Fingers crossed.

950
00:45:25,514 --> 00:45:27,015
We'll be rooting for you.

951
00:45:29,101 --> 00:45:30,728
We should probably go to bed.

952
00:45:31,687 --> 00:45:33,147
We're going to sleep, guys.

953
00:45:33,230 --> 00:45:34,773
-Okay, good night.
-Thanks.

954
00:45:34,857 --> 00:45:36,692
-Sleep well, okay?
-Night, guys.

955
00:45:36,775 --> 00:45:39,737
HYEON-SEO, SEONG-BHIN
AND YUN-WOO GO TO BED

956
00:45:40,320 --> 00:45:42,573
Shoot. We never got to see you
use the karaoke.

957
00:45:42,656 --> 00:45:44,825
So, like, do you just
go up there and sing?

958
00:45:45,409 --> 00:45:47,745
-Can we use it?
-Sure, go ahead.

959
00:45:47,828 --> 00:45:50,706
-Boss? Boss?
-Huh?

960
00:45:50,789 --> 00:45:52,374
-What?
-He wants to sing a song.

961
00:45:54,543 --> 00:45:55,878
Yeah, go sing a song, then.

962
00:45:56,462 --> 00:45:58,130
ENTERING THE KARAOKE ROOM

963
00:46:00,215 --> 00:46:02,050
-Going solo.
-I love that he's doing it alone.

964
00:46:02,134 --> 00:46:04,136
It's nice, like there's background music.

965
00:46:04,219 --> 00:46:06,180
Everyone's doing their own thing.

966
00:46:06,680 --> 00:46:08,766
-We'll close this. Probably.
-Should we?

967
00:46:09,641 --> 00:46:11,894
WITHOUT A TIME LIMIT

968
00:46:12,478 --> 00:46:16,273
KARAOKE IS RUNNING AT FULL CAPACITY

969
00:46:16,356 --> 00:46:18,567
They're really making the most of it.

970
00:46:18,650 --> 00:46:20,861
Yeah, I'm glad
they're putting it to good use.

971
00:46:20,944 --> 00:46:21,987
Cheers.

972
00:46:23,947 --> 00:46:25,616
-Having fun?
-Yes.

973
00:46:25,699 --> 00:46:27,785
How do you feel?
Can you believe it's the last day?

974
00:46:27,868 --> 00:46:30,579
Yeah, well, I was feeling
sort of down in the beginning.

975
00:46:30,662 --> 00:46:31,789
Why's that?

976
00:46:32,414 --> 00:46:34,792
When I was younger,
I had fun meeting strangers,

977
00:46:34,875 --> 00:46:37,294
but somehow it got harder for me.

978
00:46:37,377 --> 00:46:39,421
Have you been disappointed by them?

979
00:46:39,505 --> 00:46:43,717
No, I think I became numb to it.
Yeah, like, when it's your main objective.

980
00:46:43,801 --> 00:46:46,178
From our perspective,
everything is shiny and new.

981
00:46:46,261 --> 00:46:48,889
-Right.
-You're hosting for a long time.

982
00:46:48,972 --> 00:46:50,599
Yeah, I think I just put a wall up.

983
00:46:50,682 --> 00:46:53,018
It just takes me longer
to connect with people.

984
00:46:53,101 --> 00:46:56,355
Anyway, with Kian's B&B, I was worried.

985
00:46:56,438 --> 00:46:58,732
"Can I be genuine while meeting people?"

986
00:46:58,816 --> 00:47:01,485
But I've never had
to fake any excitement on the show.

987
00:47:01,568 --> 00:47:04,905
It's just, I'm giving it my all
and trying not to perform too much.

988
00:47:04,988 --> 00:47:08,867
I wasn't sure if it was the right fit
for me to be a host on a show like this,

989
00:47:08,951 --> 00:47:10,744
but as time went on,

990
00:47:10,828 --> 00:47:15,457
I eased into it and felt more comfortable
welcoming people here.

991
00:47:15,541 --> 00:47:16,959
HE GREW MORE AT EASE AS TIME PASSED

992
00:47:17,042 --> 00:47:20,504
I just need to not get stuck in my head
and in the day-to-day,

993
00:47:20,587 --> 00:47:24,341
and, you know, be more present.

994
00:47:24,424 --> 00:47:27,427
But overall, I'm happy.
I should be having fun, right?

995
00:47:28,971 --> 00:47:31,265
When I was younger,
I used to really love people watching.

996
00:47:31,348 --> 00:47:32,266
Yeah, I just…

997
00:47:32,349 --> 00:47:34,518
I had an interest in observing people

998
00:47:34,601 --> 00:47:37,104
and wondering
what kind of lives they lived. But…

999
00:47:38,230 --> 00:47:40,357
Yeah, I had a lot
of empathy and affection…

1000
00:47:41,275 --> 00:47:43,402
for my fellow human beings.

1001
00:47:43,485 --> 00:47:45,445
But as I've gotten older,

1002
00:47:45,529 --> 00:47:48,949
I think my curiosity for others
has kind of dampened.

1003
00:47:52,911 --> 00:47:54,955
Oh, man, why is this so hard now?

1004
00:47:55,038 --> 00:47:57,833
So I wondered, you know, "Have I changed?"

1005
00:47:58,458 --> 00:48:03,130
And even though I was taken aback
by the comment that I was serious or dark…

1006
00:48:03,213 --> 00:48:05,132
I realized something
because of Smita today.

1007
00:48:05,215 --> 00:48:08,093
Are you worried that you're coming off
as stressed out to the guests?

1008
00:48:08,176 --> 00:48:11,054
-I think so. I need to keep it light.
-Maybe.

1009
00:48:11,763 --> 00:48:16,393
It's nice to meet you, oh, yeah

1010
00:48:17,728 --> 00:48:18,854
Yeah

1011
00:48:19,813 --> 00:48:21,732
-Cheers!
-Cheers!

1012
00:48:22,900 --> 00:48:23,901
Glad you're here.

1013
00:48:24,568 --> 00:48:27,487
Please enjoy yourselves.
Have fun before you leave.

1014
00:48:28,405 --> 00:48:31,450
But as I kept doing it over and over,
eventually I found…

1015
00:48:32,409 --> 00:48:34,494
Yeah, I was able to loosen up.

1016
00:48:34,578 --> 00:48:36,955
And it was really thanks to the guests.

1017
00:48:37,956 --> 00:48:41,835
I felt safer to come out of my shell
a little more each day.

1018
00:48:41,919 --> 00:48:43,837
It's so cold!

1019
00:48:45,380 --> 00:48:49,009
They were so understanding and generous
and let me open up.

1020
00:48:52,846 --> 00:48:55,057
You know, when I think about it,
I keep getting choked up,

1021
00:48:55,140 --> 00:48:56,642
just replaying it in my head.

1022
00:48:57,267 --> 00:48:58,894
The most important thing is,

1023
00:49:00,062 --> 00:49:03,357
I thought my heart had grown cold
or hopeless, but I think…

1024
00:49:04,107 --> 00:49:06,818
I was able to develop
some really genuine connections.

1025
00:49:06,902 --> 00:49:09,905
So as time went on,
that heart exterior cracked.

1026
00:49:10,906 --> 00:49:14,034
Trust me, Kian,
we like you and think you're social.

1027
00:49:14,117 --> 00:49:17,204
Oh, well, thanks.
You know, people actually do like me…

1028
00:49:18,038 --> 00:49:20,248
This just makes me blush.
All right, let's have a drink.

1029
00:49:22,125 --> 00:49:23,794
-Nice timing.
-Best of luck to everybody.

1030
00:49:23,877 --> 00:49:25,337
-Thank you.
-And to you as well.

1031
00:49:25,420 --> 00:49:26,797
Cheers.

1032
00:49:29,007 --> 00:49:31,635
I think I'm off to bed.
Have a great night, everyone.

1033
00:49:31,718 --> 00:49:33,345
-Going to sleep like that?
-Huh?

1034
00:49:33,428 --> 00:49:35,222
-Wash up first.
-I'll do it in the morning.

1035
00:49:35,305 --> 00:49:37,557
What, I'm just going to get dirty again.

1036
00:49:37,641 --> 00:49:39,476
You guys are crazy. You shower too much.

1037
00:49:39,559 --> 00:49:40,769
KIAN'S B&B

1038
00:49:40,852 --> 00:49:44,564
DAY 9

1039
00:49:44,648 --> 00:49:47,192
CLOSING DAY

1040
00:49:47,275 --> 00:49:50,946
CLEAR SKIES ON THE MORNING OF THE LAST DAY

1041
00:49:56,159 --> 00:49:58,620
KIAN'S B&B WINTERVILLE

1042
00:50:01,498 --> 00:50:04,167
3 HOURS BEFORE CLOSING

1043
00:50:04,251 --> 00:50:05,585
8:00 A.M.

1044
00:50:08,130 --> 00:50:10,382
JUN-HO'S THE FIRST TO GET UP
ON THE LAST DAY TOO

1045
00:50:10,465 --> 00:50:12,551
YEON-KOUNG AND ZUHA
ARE SLEEPING SIDE BY SIDE

1046
00:50:16,346 --> 00:50:19,599
THEY GET UP AT THE SAME TIME

1047
00:50:22,102 --> 00:50:24,187
THEY PUT AWAY THEIR BEDDING TOGETHER

1048
00:50:24,271 --> 00:50:25,981
AND PACK TOGETHER

1049
00:50:31,153 --> 00:50:33,280
Do you think you'll cry today?

1050
00:50:34,322 --> 00:50:37,576
Don't cry, Zuha.

1051
00:50:37,659 --> 00:50:39,745
THE BOSS IS PACKING UP TOO

1052
00:50:39,828 --> 00:50:40,954
HE PACKS THE TOWEL HE USED

1053
00:50:41,038 --> 00:50:42,622
I need new socks.

1054
00:50:47,919 --> 00:50:49,713
PUTTING ON SOCKS AFTER SMELLING THEM

1055
00:50:51,423 --> 00:50:54,051
HIS SUIT WORN AT THE PARTY

1056
00:50:54,718 --> 00:50:56,303
A SWEATSHIRT

1057
00:50:57,054 --> 00:50:58,972
AND A LONG PADDED JACKET

1058
00:50:59,848 --> 00:51:01,892
HE FINISHES PACKING ALL CLOTHES
FROM THE 9-DAY STAY

1059
00:51:02,476 --> 00:51:04,352
-You only got to enjoy it for half a day.
-Yes.

1060
00:51:04,436 --> 00:51:06,104
-Was it still fun?
-It was so much fun.

1061
00:51:06,855 --> 00:51:08,148
I'm so glad.

1062
00:51:08,231 --> 00:51:09,232
10:00 A.M.

1063
00:51:09,316 --> 00:51:11,068
It's already 10:00. Time to check out.

1064
00:51:11,151 --> 00:51:12,444
So it's time to leave.

1065
00:51:13,612 --> 00:51:14,821
I think it's over.

1066
00:51:14,905 --> 00:51:15,906
It is.

1067
00:51:16,406 --> 00:51:18,575
This time we're leaving with everyone.

1068
00:51:18,658 --> 00:51:22,245
-So it just feels like super weird.
-Yeah.

1069
00:51:22,329 --> 00:51:23,497
THE STAFF FEEL RESTLESS TOO

1070
00:51:23,580 --> 00:51:26,666
But sleeping in our own beds…

1071
00:51:26,750 --> 00:51:28,502
I'm excited, but sad.

1072
00:51:29,586 --> 00:51:31,338
Thank you guys for coming to visit.

1073
00:51:33,215 --> 00:51:35,550
Let's just all stay.

1074
00:51:35,634 --> 00:51:36,968
We don't want to leave.

1075
00:51:37,052 --> 00:51:38,345
-Yeah?
-We'll just move in.

1076
00:51:38,929 --> 00:51:40,931
All right, before you go,
we'll hang these up.

1077
00:51:41,014 --> 00:51:43,350
-Okay.
-For the last time, right?

1078
00:51:44,142 --> 00:51:45,143
SOMEWHAT EMOTIONAL?

1079
00:51:45,227 --> 00:51:46,353
Hard to say goodbye?

1080
00:51:46,436 --> 00:51:47,646
We'll try not to cry.

1081
00:51:47,729 --> 00:51:49,439
You can inspire them
by saying, "Be happy!"

1082
00:51:49,523 --> 00:51:51,483
Yeah, be happy. Uh…

1083
00:51:52,692 --> 00:51:54,194
Oh, be careful up there, guys.

1084
00:51:54,694 --> 00:51:57,531
Wow, you're working for us
right before you go?

1085
00:51:57,614 --> 00:51:59,032
-You can just throw them.
-Okay.

1086
00:51:59,116 --> 00:52:01,243
-We can pass the hangers down.
-Okay.

1087
00:52:01,326 --> 00:52:03,954
-Pull it all the way so it fits.
-Cool.

1088
00:52:04,037 --> 00:52:05,330
WORKING TOGETHER TO HANG THEM

1089
00:52:05,413 --> 00:52:06,748
-I'll help.
-I got it.

1090
00:52:06,832 --> 00:52:08,250
Teamwork, teamwork.

1091
00:52:08,333 --> 00:52:10,794
-Let's make it look good.
-Yeah, one sec.

1092
00:52:11,378 --> 00:52:12,337
Okay.

1093
00:52:12,420 --> 00:52:14,548
-Looks good, guys.
-Much better than on the floor.

1094
00:52:15,507 --> 00:52:17,884
Let's take a group photo.
Is the angle okay?

1095
00:52:17,968 --> 00:52:18,969
SETTING THE TIMER

1096
00:52:19,052 --> 00:52:21,012
-Are we all looking good, boss?
-Of course.

1097
00:52:21,096 --> 00:52:22,848
-It's on a timer.
-Okay.

1098
00:52:22,931 --> 00:52:24,558
-Quickly.
-Everyone, smile.

1099
00:52:26,226 --> 00:52:28,019
One, two, three…

1100
00:52:28,103 --> 00:52:31,231
WITH THE LAST GUESTS

1101
00:52:32,190 --> 00:52:34,484
Okay, we really have to go now.

1102
00:52:35,360 --> 00:52:37,195
I'll be rooting for you.

1103
00:52:37,279 --> 00:52:38,864
-I hope everything goes well.
-We had fun.

1104
00:52:38,947 --> 00:52:41,032
-Goodbye. Be safe.
-Thank you.

1105
00:52:41,116 --> 00:52:42,325
-Thank you.
-Bye.

1106
00:52:46,663 --> 00:52:49,207
This place is challenging up to the end.

1107
00:52:49,291 --> 00:52:50,876
-Are we stuck?
-Snow's blocking the door.

1108
00:52:50,959 --> 00:52:52,043
Can we get out?

1109
00:52:52,627 --> 00:52:54,254
I think it's because the snow fell.

1110
00:52:54,337 --> 00:52:55,338
THE BOSS GOES OUT

1111
00:52:56,131 --> 00:52:57,132
I will not miss this door.

1112
00:52:57,215 --> 00:52:59,342
-We could bring the suitcases out.
-Oh, true.

1113
00:52:59,426 --> 00:53:02,137
THEY ESCAPE ONE BY ONE

1114
00:53:02,220 --> 00:53:04,181
-Hope to see you.
-Goodbye for real, guys.

1115
00:53:04,264 --> 00:53:05,849
-Thanks again.
-Time to go home.

1116
00:53:05,932 --> 00:53:07,142
-Goodbye!
-See you.

1117
00:53:07,225 --> 00:53:08,560
-Safe travels.
-Bye.

1118
00:53:08,643 --> 00:53:10,812
-Off we go.
-Off we go.

1119
00:53:10,896 --> 00:53:12,898
The snow stopped
as soon as we had to leave.

1120
00:53:12,981 --> 00:53:15,650
Right? It let up just in time
for us to get home.

1121
00:53:15,734 --> 00:53:18,236
So, in ice climbing,
being the first person to step

1122
00:53:18,320 --> 00:53:20,739
on untouched snow is called "onsight."

1123
00:53:21,323 --> 00:53:22,908
Getting to play in the snow and have fun

1124
00:53:22,991 --> 00:53:25,076
made this trip
feel like a new start for me.

1125
00:53:25,160 --> 00:53:27,329
I didn't realize
truly how much I needed it.

1126
00:53:28,330 --> 00:53:30,081
I'm in love with that trampoline.

1127
00:53:30,165 --> 00:53:32,375
When you become an adult,
something so silly and fun

1128
00:53:32,459 --> 00:53:34,002
becomes a thing you don't do.

1129
00:53:34,085 --> 00:53:37,047
So I thought Kian's B&B
was like a playground for adults.

1130
00:53:38,757 --> 00:53:42,260
At a typical B&B, it's usually
easiest to do everything by myself.

1131
00:53:42,344 --> 00:53:43,845
But at Kian's B&B,

1132
00:53:43,929 --> 00:53:46,640
there were physical challenges
that made sure we worked together

1133
00:53:46,723 --> 00:53:47,849
and helped each other.

1134
00:53:47,933 --> 00:53:50,060
Out of all the guests
to visit this season,

1135
00:53:50,143 --> 00:53:51,686
we were the youngest by a lot.

1136
00:53:51,770 --> 00:53:54,856
But everyone older than us
was so thoughtful and kind to us.

1137
00:53:55,440 --> 00:53:57,567
I was able to forget about things

1138
00:53:57,651 --> 00:53:59,152
that stressed me out, like school.

1139
00:53:59,236 --> 00:54:03,031
And I got to have a ton of fun,
which was such an amazing experience.

1140
00:54:03,114 --> 00:54:05,700
It was only one night,
but it was so magical.

1141
00:54:05,784 --> 00:54:07,077
I'll remember it for a long time.

1142
00:54:07,160 --> 00:54:10,664
-It's one of my fondest memories so far.
-I think it deserves a ten out of ten.

1143
00:54:11,581 --> 00:54:14,167
-The house is even saying bye to us.
-That's right.

1144
00:54:15,794 --> 00:54:18,463
-Don't forget about us.
-Definitely keep in touch.

1145
00:54:19,047 --> 00:54:20,048
Okay.

1146
00:54:20,131 --> 00:54:22,676
THE LAST GUESTS CHECK OUT

1147
00:54:24,010 --> 00:54:26,846
The last guests have left.

1148
00:54:28,181 --> 00:54:30,725
-It was a good send-off.
-Let's clean up. One last time.

1149
00:54:30,809 --> 00:54:31,810
Fine.

1150
00:54:32,394 --> 00:54:34,479
-I'll sweep there.
-Okay.

1151
00:54:34,980 --> 00:54:38,358
-Then never again, thank God.
-So the day to leave is finally upon us.

1152
00:54:38,441 --> 00:54:39,651
THE LAST CLEANUP OF KIAN'S B&B

1153
00:54:40,235 --> 00:54:42,821
-Feels so weird, right?
-I know.

1154
00:54:43,405 --> 00:54:45,699
It's the last time
we're gonna see this place.

1155
00:54:46,616 --> 00:54:48,868
It's the last time I fold these.

1156
00:54:50,036 --> 00:54:51,371
Almost done. Almost done.

1157
00:54:56,209 --> 00:55:00,588
CLEANUP LIST
BREAK DOWN THE PULLEY

1158
00:55:01,172 --> 00:55:03,925
Yeon-koung? Sorry.
But can you hand me the snacks?

1159
00:55:04,009 --> 00:55:05,302
Be better if we leave them here.

1160
00:55:05,385 --> 00:55:07,304
CLEANUP LIST
GATHER LEFTOVER SNACKS IN THE KITCHEN

1161
00:55:07,887 --> 00:55:09,514
-Can you lift it?
-Yeah.

1162
00:55:10,223 --> 00:55:11,308
GETS INTO POSITION

1163
00:55:11,391 --> 00:55:13,852
-Now be careful.
-Is this smart?

1164
00:55:13,935 --> 00:55:16,855
Wait, wait, wait.
Can you lift this side up a bit?

1165
00:55:16,938 --> 00:55:18,398
Yeah, lift it.

1166
00:55:18,982 --> 00:55:21,109
-You got it?
-Slowly.

1167
00:55:21,609 --> 00:55:22,944
Okay.

1168
00:55:23,028 --> 00:55:24,321
-Nope.
-Oh, no.

1169
00:55:24,404 --> 00:55:25,947
Wait, wait, wait. Grab it.

1170
00:55:26,031 --> 00:55:28,700
-Okay.
-Grab it before it falls.

1171
00:55:28,783 --> 00:55:30,201
Shit.

1172
00:55:32,078 --> 00:55:33,163
A BIZARRE MESS UNTIL THE END

1173
00:55:33,246 --> 00:55:34,873
What a total mess, you guys.

1174
00:55:37,751 --> 00:55:39,085
Where's the dolly?

1175
00:55:39,878 --> 00:55:41,171
I already took it apart.

1176
00:55:41,796 --> 00:55:42,797
Oh, you did?

1177
00:55:43,548 --> 00:55:45,133
-Yeah.
-Try this. Here, here, here.

1178
00:55:45,216 --> 00:55:46,384
Can we use that?

1179
00:55:46,468 --> 00:55:48,386
Yeon-koung, I'm sorry, but…

1180
00:55:48,470 --> 00:55:50,722
-Can you put them in this, and lift it up?
-Oh, come on.

1181
00:55:53,850 --> 00:55:54,851
Wait a second.

1182
00:55:55,560 --> 00:55:57,562
Okay. Should have done that first.

1183
00:55:58,396 --> 00:55:59,856
-Thank you.
-Okay.

1184
00:56:02,067 --> 00:56:03,026
Ta-da.

1185
00:56:03,109 --> 00:56:04,486
THE KITCHEN IS NEATLY ORGANIZED

1186
00:56:05,070 --> 00:56:07,489
-Shouldn't we…
-I'll just put this box in there…

1187
00:56:08,031 --> 00:56:09,032
Do it together.

1188
00:56:10,408 --> 00:56:11,451
THIS TIME, THE BOX IS…

1189
00:56:11,534 --> 00:56:12,535
Are you okay there?

1190
00:56:14,537 --> 00:56:15,789
Can we help you carry that out?

1191
00:56:15,872 --> 00:56:17,040
STUCK

1192
00:56:17,123 --> 00:56:20,293
Don't pull so hard, you'll rip it.

1193
00:56:26,925 --> 00:56:27,926
BARELY ESCAPES

1194
00:56:28,009 --> 00:56:31,346
Oh, so how do we do this?
This would happen right at the end.

1195
00:56:32,180 --> 00:56:35,183
-It won't budge? Then just go.
-I can carry it out if I squish it.

1196
00:56:35,266 --> 00:56:37,602
-Here goes. Halfway there.
-It'll work, it'll work.

1197
00:56:38,395 --> 00:56:40,563
Oh, what the?

1198
00:56:42,816 --> 00:56:44,526
-Did it burst?
-You come out first, Jun-ho.

1199
00:56:44,609 --> 00:56:47,654
It ripped open.
It's okay, it's okay, it's okay.

1200
00:56:47,737 --> 00:56:50,198
-It's all spilling out now.
-To the very end.

1201
00:56:51,658 --> 00:56:53,535
PICKING UP THE FALLEN TRASH

1202
00:56:53,618 --> 00:56:55,703
Yeah, yeah, stupid door's annoying.

1203
00:56:55,787 --> 00:56:58,039
You can't check in now
even if you want to.

1204
00:56:58,123 --> 00:56:59,874
THEY SORT RECYCLABLES
FOR THE LAST TIME TOO

1205
00:56:59,958 --> 00:57:01,084
Is that all the trash?

1206
00:57:01,876 --> 00:57:03,628
I think we have all of it.

1207
00:57:05,046 --> 00:57:06,631
-I think we're done.
-Thank God.

1208
00:57:06,714 --> 00:57:07,674
THE LAST CLEANUP IS OVER

1209
00:57:07,757 --> 00:57:10,718
-We should write something.
-Sounds good. Let's all write.

1210
00:57:11,302 --> 00:57:12,720
Hey, what about the painting?

1211
00:57:13,513 --> 00:57:15,098
-Kian, your painting!
-Our mini Yeon-koung

1212
00:57:16,141 --> 00:57:19,436
Oh, man, it looks so weird
that your face is the only one up there.

1213
00:57:20,103 --> 00:57:21,479
Who cares?

1214
00:57:21,563 --> 00:57:24,858
-I didn't have time to do more. I guess.
-Will it be all right with just her?

1215
00:57:24,941 --> 00:57:27,318
JUN-HO & KIAN

1216
00:57:28,611 --> 00:57:31,281
-Kazuha wrote the longest message.
-For real?

1217
00:57:31,364 --> 00:57:34,284
"The people I met here,
the time we spent together…"

1218
00:57:34,367 --> 00:57:38,288
"They're truly precious
treasures and have changed my life."

1219
00:57:38,371 --> 00:57:40,457
Oh, she wrote that you're amazing.

1220
00:57:40,540 --> 00:57:41,916
KIAN'S B&B'S BOSS IS THE BEST!

1221
00:57:42,000 --> 00:57:43,293
Did you know she thinks that?

1222
00:57:43,376 --> 00:57:44,502
You're amazing.

1223
00:57:44,586 --> 00:57:46,713
HAPPY

1224
00:57:47,297 --> 00:57:48,298
-Zuha.
-Yeah?

1225
00:57:48,381 --> 00:57:50,049
Who told you to lie like that?

1226
00:57:50,800 --> 00:57:53,136
-Be real with him.
-She knows I'm not lying.

1227
00:57:53,219 --> 00:57:54,679
-Why doubt her sincerity?
-Zuha.

1228
00:57:54,762 --> 00:57:56,055
She's telling the truth.

1229
00:57:57,724 --> 00:58:00,393
-Do you need help?
-No, thanks.

1230
00:58:01,186 --> 00:58:03,271
-Let's go!
-Goodbye.

1231
00:58:03,354 --> 00:58:04,814
So long, B&B.

1232
00:58:04,898 --> 00:58:06,566
When I see the empty house like this,

1233
00:58:06,649 --> 00:58:08,401
it kind of seems like it flew by.

1234
00:58:09,152 --> 00:58:11,112
-Well, it's time to go.
-All right.

1235
00:58:11,196 --> 00:58:12,614
IT WAS GREAT MEETING SO MANY PEOPLE

1236
00:58:12,697 --> 00:58:14,240
THANK YOU FOR THE MEMORIES
BREAD UNNIE

1237
00:58:15,200 --> 00:58:16,159
We're heading out!

1238
00:58:16,242 --> 00:58:17,494
THANK YOU FOR BEAUTIFUL MEMORIES

1239
00:58:17,577 --> 00:58:18,578
GOOD JOB, EVERYONE
KAZUHA

1240
00:58:18,661 --> 00:58:19,662
I WANT TO THANK EVERYONE

1241
00:58:19,746 --> 00:58:20,663
FOR THE MEMORIES
JUN-HO

1242
00:58:20,747 --> 00:58:22,749
-To be going home?
-Uh-huh.

1243
00:58:23,875 --> 00:58:25,919
-The weather is beautiful.
-It really is.

1244
00:58:26,794 --> 00:58:29,881
It's so sunny.
Today's the best weather we've had.

1245
00:58:29,964 --> 00:58:32,217
Figures that it happens the day we leave.

1246
00:58:32,300 --> 00:58:34,219
Do we think the boss is…

1247
00:58:34,302 --> 00:58:36,346
-saying one last prayer inside?
-Praying?

1248
00:58:36,429 --> 00:58:38,097
-Hopefully, quickly.
-Oh…

1249
00:58:39,432 --> 00:58:40,433
Last time.

1250
00:58:43,228 --> 00:58:45,480
TURNING THE LIGHTS OFF FOR THE LAST TIME

1251
00:58:54,030 --> 00:58:55,406
Man, this is so weird.

1252
00:59:20,807 --> 00:59:24,811
REMEMBERING MOMENTS WE CAN'T GO BACK TO
KIAN84

1253
00:59:24,894 --> 00:59:28,731
With everybody gone, it just feels weird
to be cleaning up an empty place.

1254
00:59:29,941 --> 00:59:31,985
But once it was clean
and we were walking out,

1255
00:59:32,068 --> 00:59:33,319
I kept looking back.

1256
00:59:33,403 --> 00:59:34,445
I thought to myself,

1257
00:59:34,529 --> 00:59:35,947
"What if this was my actual home

1258
00:59:36,030 --> 00:59:37,865
and the people who came
were my real friends?"

1259
00:59:37,949 --> 00:59:40,952
I started to daydream
about that being true.

1260
00:59:43,121 --> 00:59:45,456
These kind of experiences
aren't built to last.

1261
00:59:47,166 --> 00:59:49,877
You know how flowers are the prettiest
when they first bloom,

1262
00:59:49,961 --> 00:59:52,797
but then they suddenly just wither away?

1263
00:59:52,880 --> 00:59:54,549
This place was kind of like that.

1264
00:59:55,633 --> 00:59:58,303
When I thought about
leaving this place for good, I…

1265
00:59:59,137 --> 01:00:01,889
felt like you do when you wake up
too soon from a dream.

1266
01:00:02,557 --> 01:00:04,892
This place taught me how to be present,

1267
01:00:04,976 --> 01:00:07,937
and also how to take an interest
in others.

1268
01:00:09,063 --> 01:00:12,233
After I retired, I was trying to find
my new purpose in life,

1269
01:00:12,317 --> 01:00:16,321
and I think I neglected the small joys,
friendship, rest, fun, travel.

1270
01:00:17,238 --> 01:00:20,074
I think I totally lost track
of what life is really about.

1271
01:00:20,158 --> 01:00:22,493
Oh, my God! This is fun!

1272
01:00:22,577 --> 01:00:26,789
But I reconnected with those
important things while at Kian's B&B.

1273
01:00:27,457 --> 01:00:31,044
Spending eight nights and nine days
welcoming guests here…

1274
01:00:31,794 --> 01:00:35,590
Yeah, that's the dream
that Kian kept talking about.

1275
01:00:36,090 --> 01:00:39,344
I was able to see that vision
shining through other people,

1276
01:00:39,427 --> 01:00:41,054
like a mirror almost.

1277
01:00:41,596 --> 01:00:44,015
This really was a precious experience.

1278
01:00:44,807 --> 01:00:48,061
Okay.

1279
01:00:48,144 --> 01:00:50,355
We may all be going
in different directions,

1280
01:00:50,438 --> 01:00:53,858
but meeting so many people
who do a lot of different things,

1281
01:00:53,941 --> 01:00:56,903
it was energizing
because they're all pros.

1282
01:00:56,986 --> 01:00:58,946
They're the best at what they do.

1283
01:00:59,030 --> 01:01:00,156
I kept thinking to myself,

1284
01:01:00,239 --> 01:01:03,201
"I should work a little bit harder
when I get home."

1285
01:01:03,284 --> 01:01:05,078
It went by really fast, but I loved it,

1286
01:01:05,161 --> 01:01:07,789
and I think it had
a really positive impact on me.

1287
01:01:11,668 --> 01:01:12,752
THE 2ND B&B IS CLOSED

1288
01:01:12,835 --> 01:01:14,253
-It's officially closed.
-Bye, house.

1289
01:01:14,337 --> 01:01:16,464
-No!
-Well, great work, everyone.

1290
01:01:16,547 --> 01:01:18,549
We did it.

1291
01:01:18,633 --> 01:01:20,677
-Now let's go.
-Let's get out of here.

1292
01:01:21,344 --> 01:01:23,137
-Oh, wow.
-We did it!

1293
01:01:24,389 --> 01:01:26,307
-Does it feel weird to be done?
-So weird.

1294
01:01:26,391 --> 01:01:28,851
-I feel like I have to come back tomorrow.
-Yeah.

1295
01:01:29,769 --> 01:01:31,729
And, of course, this walk is so long.

1296
01:01:31,813 --> 01:01:33,690
-Hard until the end.
-Guys, don't ever forget.

1297
01:01:33,773 --> 01:01:35,608
Hopes and dreams.

1298
01:01:37,610 --> 01:01:39,779
All right, let's get out of here.

1299
01:01:40,655 --> 01:01:41,864
I'll miss it here.

1300
01:01:46,869 --> 01:01:48,287
Let's try this.

1301
01:01:48,371 --> 01:01:50,164
But I'm really bad at it.

1302
01:01:50,248 --> 01:01:52,500
-Want me to hold the net?
-This net is great.

1303
01:01:52,583 --> 01:01:54,877
If we hit this ten times back and forth,

1304
01:01:54,961 --> 01:01:57,255
Kian's B&B will be a huge hit.

1305
01:01:57,338 --> 01:01:59,966
-Oh, please, I don't want to.
-Season 2 will be a huge hit.

1306
01:02:00,049 --> 01:02:03,136
But if we fail and the ball falls down,
then Kian's B&B will be in trouble.

1307
01:02:03,219 --> 01:02:06,055
-Hey, don't joke about that.
-And then we'll have to close down.

1308
01:02:06,139 --> 01:02:07,765
No, I'm kind of superstitious.

1309
01:02:08,599 --> 01:02:10,351
This is for the future of Season 2!

1310
01:02:10,435 --> 01:02:12,103
-Okay.
-Our goal is ten.

1311
01:02:12,729 --> 01:02:15,022
One, two, three…

1312
01:02:16,524 --> 01:02:17,734
You don't have to smack it.

1313
01:02:18,860 --> 01:02:22,739
-You have to do ten, okay? One, two…
-That's it!

1314
01:02:23,448 --> 01:02:24,991
Looks like we're in trouble.

1315
01:02:25,074 --> 01:02:27,118
-Hey!
-What?

1316
01:02:27,201 --> 01:02:28,703
Zuha, don't mess this up.

1317
01:02:29,203 --> 01:02:31,247
Let's give it a shot. No regrets.

1318
01:02:34,250 --> 01:02:36,711
-Two, three,
-That's it, that's it.

1319
01:02:36,794 --> 01:02:38,629
-four, five,
-Keep it up, guys.

1320
01:02:38,713 --> 01:02:40,715
six, seven, eight…

1321
01:02:42,717 --> 01:02:44,427
-nine, ten!
-Nine…

1322
01:02:44,510 --> 01:02:47,054
Hey, it's got to be underhand. No!

1323
01:02:49,891 --> 01:02:50,892
Nice try, though.

1324
01:02:51,559 --> 01:02:53,644
Hey, we have to do ten. We were at nine.

1325
01:02:54,228 --> 01:02:56,522
We have to do it. We have to.
Let's go, let's go.

1326
01:02:56,606 --> 01:02:57,982
-One…
-One, two,

1327
01:02:58,065 --> 01:03:00,318
-three, four, five…
-Three, four, five…

1328
01:03:01,694 --> 01:03:03,571
six, seven,

1329
01:03:03,654 --> 01:03:04,655
-eight…
-Eight!

1330
01:03:04,739 --> 01:03:05,948
Almost there.

1331
01:03:06,032 --> 01:03:07,283
Nine…

1332
01:03:07,909 --> 01:03:09,911
-Nine…
-Ten! We did it!

1333
01:03:09,994 --> 01:03:13,998
-Nine…
-Ten! Yeah, we did it!

1334
01:03:14,081 --> 01:03:16,334
Kian's B&B is going to be a hit.

1335
01:03:17,335 --> 01:03:19,545
Great job. You're good at that.

1336
01:03:20,129 --> 01:03:22,006
-All right, you did it.
-Sure did, boss!

1337
01:03:22,089 --> 01:03:23,883
That was so intense.

1338
01:03:23,966 --> 01:03:24,967
Good job.

1339
01:03:26,177 --> 01:03:28,221
By the skin of our teeth,
but we're going to be a hit.

1340
01:03:28,304 --> 01:03:29,847
-We will.
-We did it.
